<title>FRANCE: Gascogne buys Cegepac from CDR.</title>
<headline>Gascogne buys Cegepac from CDR.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Paper maker Groupe Gascogne said it had agreed with CDR Entreprises to acquire a 96.78 percent stake in Cegepac of France and 100 percent of Embalco in Belgium for an undisclosed sum.</p>
<p>Both companies make packaging machines and had combined 1995 sales of 384 million francs and a net profit of 5.4 million.</p>
<p>CDR is an investment vehicle set-up to sell former Credit Lyonnais assets.</p>
</text>
